{"id":"28b7923416cd37e4","group":"58","path":"58/batch18/58-thm-lax-milgram.md","title":"Lax–Milgram Theorem","display":"thm-lax-milgram — Lax–Milgram Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-lax-milgram","aliases":["58-thm-lax-milgram"],"display":"thm-lax-milgram — Lax–Milgram Theorem","depends_on":["[[../batch13/58-df-hilbert-space.md]]","[[../batch06/58-df-linear-map.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-lax-milgram"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-lax-milgram</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-lax-milgram — Lax–Milgram Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"b70ce791d5b1a19b\" href=\"?note=b70ce791d5b1a19b\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-hilbert-space.md\">../batch13/58-df-hilbert-space.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"f67456d74b418241\" href=\"?note=f67456d74b418241\" title=\"../batch06/58-df-linear-map.md\">../batch06/58-df-linear-map.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"V,B,\\mathbb F,+_V,\\cdot_V,+_{\\mathbb F},\\cdot_{\\mathbb F},a,f,\\alpha,C,r_f\\in V\">\\(V,B,\\mathbb F,+_V,\\cdot_V,+_{\\mathbb F},\\cdot_{\\mathbb F},a,f,\\alpha,C,r_f\\in V\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb F\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}\">\\(\\mathbb F\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(V,B,\\mathbb F,+_V,\\cdot_V)\">\\(\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(V,B,\\mathbb F,+_V,\\cdot_V)\\)</span> is the imported exact five-place Hilbert-space predicate</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\nu_B(v)=\\sqrt{B(v,v)}\">\\(\\nu_B(v)=\\sqrt{B(v,v)}\\)</span> is the induced Hilbert norm</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{LinearMap}_S\\subseteq V^8\">\\(\\mathrm{LinearMap}_S\\subseteq V^8\\)</span> is the imported explicit linear-map predicate</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"+_{\\mathbb F},\\cdot_{\\mathbb F}\">\\(+_{\\mathbb F},\\cdot_{\\mathbb F}\\)</span> are the standard field operations, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Re}_{\\mathbb F}\">\\(\\operatorname{Re}_{\\mathbb F}\\)</span> is the identity on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb R\">\\(\\mathbb R\\)</span> and the real-part map on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb C\">\\(\\mathbb C\\)</span></li>\n<li>The sesquilinear convention is conjugate-linear in the first variable and linear in the second, so <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"a(u,\\cdot)\">\\(a(u,\\cdot)\\)</span> and the functional <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f\">\\(f\\)</span> have the same linearity convention</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}lax\\text{-}milgram}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathbb F\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}\n\\land\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(V,B,\\mathbb F,+_V,\\cdot_V)\n\\land a\\in\\mathbb F^{V\\times V}\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall u,v,w\\in V\\;\\forall\\lambda\\in\\mathbb F\\;\\Bigl(\na(\\lambda u+v,w)=\\overline\\lambda\\,a(u,w)+a(v,w)\n\\land a(u,\\lambda v+w)=\\lambda a(u,v)+a(u,w)\\Bigr)\n\\land C\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\n\\land\\alpha\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\n\\land\\forall u,v\\in V\\;\\bigl(|a(u,v)|\\leq C\\nu_B(u)\\nu_B(v)\\bigr)\n\\land\\forall v\\in V\\;\\bigl(\\operatorname{Re}_{\\mathbb F}a(v,v)\\geq\\alpha\\nu_B(v)^2\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\to\\forall f\\in\\mathbb F^{V}\\;\\forall r_f\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{LinearMap}_S(f,V,\\mathbb F,\\mathbb F,+_V,\\cdot_V,+_{\\mathbb F},\\cdot_{\\mathbb F})\n\\land\\forall v\\in V\\;(|f(v)|\\leq r_f\\nu_B(v))\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{9em}\\to\\exists!u\\in V\\;\\left(\n\\forall v\\in V\\;(a(u,v)=f(v))\n\\land\\nu_B(u)\\leq\\frac{r_f}{\\alpha}\\right)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}lax\\text{-}milgram}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathbb F\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}\n\\land\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(V,B,\\mathbb F,+_V,\\cdot_V)\n\\land a\\in\\mathbb F^{V\\times V}\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall u,v,w\\in V\\;\\forall\\lambda\\in\\mathbb F\\;\\Bigl(\na(\\lambda u+v,w)=\\overline\\lambda\\,a(u,w)+a(v,w)\n\\land a(u,\\lambda v+w)=\\lambda a(u,v)+a(u,w)\\Bigr)\n\\land C\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\n\\land\\alpha\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\n\\land\\forall u,v\\in V\\;\\bigl(|a(u,v)|\\leq C\\nu_B(u)\\nu_B(v)\\bigr)\n\\land\\forall v\\in V\\;\\bigl(\\operatorname{Re}_{\\mathbb F}a(v,v)\\geq\\alpha\\nu_B(v)^2\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\to\\forall f\\in\\mathbb F^{V}\\;\\forall r_f\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{LinearMap}_S(f,V,\\mathbb F,\\mathbb F,+_V,\\cdot_V,+_{\\mathbb F},\\cdot_{\\mathbb F})\n\\land\\forall v\\in V\\;(|f(v)|\\leq r_f\\nu_B(v))\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{9em}\\to\\exists!u\\in V\\;\\left(\n\\forall v\\in V\\;(a(u,v)=f(v))\n\\land\\nu_B(u)\\leq\\frac{r_f}{\\alpha}\\right)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Boundedness of the form, positivity of the coercivity constant, and the\nreal/complex sesquilinear convention are now explicit.</li>\n<li>The Hilbert predicate now receives its actual inner product, scalar field, and two vector operations.  Continuity of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f\">\\(f\\)</span> is expressed by a concrete norm bound, and the same witness <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"r_f\">\\(r_f\\)</span> controls the solution estimate.</li>\n<li>For symmetric <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"a\">\\(a\\)</span>: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"u\">\\(u\\)</span> minimizes energy <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"J(v) = \\frac{1}{2}a(v,v) - f(v)\">\\(J(v) = \\frac{1}{2}a(v,v) - f(v)\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Elliptic PDE: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"a(u,v) = \\int_\\Omega \\nabla u \\cdot \\nabla v\">\\(a(u,v) = \\int_\\Omega \\nabla u \\cdot \\nabla v\\)</span> gives Poisson equation.</li>\n<li>Babuška–Brezzi inf-sup condition generalizes coercivity.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch13/58-df-hilbert-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"b70ce791d5b1a19b","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-df-hilbert-space.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch06/58-df-linear-map.md","status":"resolved","id":"f67456d74b418241","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch06/58-df-linear-map.md]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"V,B,\\mathbb F,+_V,\\cdot_V,+_{\\mathbb F},\\cdot_{\\mathbb F},a,f,\\alpha,C,r_f\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb F\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(V,B,\\mathbb F,+_V,\\cdot_V)","display":false},{"tex":"\\nu_B(v)=\\sqrt{B(v,v)}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{LinearMap}_S\\subseteq V^8","display":false},{"tex":"+_{\\mathbb F},\\cdot_{\\mathbb F}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Re}_{\\mathbb F}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb R","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb C","display":false},{"tex":"a(u,\\cdot)","display":false},{"tex":"f","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}lax\\text{-}milgram}\\vdash{}&\n\\mathbb F\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}\n\\land\\mathrm{HilbertSpace}_S(V,B,\\mathbb F,+_V,\\cdot_V)\n\\land a\\in\\mathbb F^{V\\times V}\\\\\n&{}\\land\\forall u,v,w\\in V\\;\\forall\\lambda\\in\\mathbb F\\;\\Bigl(\na(\\lambda u+v,w)=\\overline\\lambda\\,a(u,w)+a(v,w)\n\\land a(u,\\lambda v+w)=\\lambda a(u,v)+a(u,w)\\Bigr)\n\\land C\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\n\\land\\alpha\\in\\mathbb R_{>0}\n\\land\\forall u,v\\in V\\;\\bigl(|a(u,v)|\\leq C\\nu_B(u)\\nu_B(v)\\bigr)\n\\land\\forall v\\in V\\;\\bigl(\\operatorname{Re}_{\\mathbb F}a(v,v)\\geq\\alpha\\nu_B(v)^2\\bigr)\\\\\n&\\quad\\to\\forall f\\in\\mathbb F^{V}\\;\\forall r_f\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{LinearMap}_S(f,V,\\mathbb F,\\mathbb F,+_V,\\cdot_V,+_{\\mathbb F},\\cdot_{\\mathbb F})\n\\land\\forall v\\in V\\;(|f(v)|\\leq r_f\\nu_B(v))\\\\\n&\\hspace{9em}\\to\\exists!u\\in V\\;\\left(\n\\forall v\\in V\\;(a(u,v)=f(v))\n\\land\\nu_B(u)\\leq\\frac{r_f}{\\alpha}\\right)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"f","display":false},{"tex":"r_f","display":false},{"tex":"a","display":false},{"tex":"u","display":false},{"tex":"J(v) = \\frac{1}{2}a(v,v) - f(v)","display":false},{"tex":"a(u,v) = \\int_\\Omega \\nabla u \\cdot \\nabla v","display":false}],"bytes":2585,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4275","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch18/58-thm-lax-milgram.md|58-thm-lax-milgram]]（batch18）"}],"outgoing":["b70ce791d5b1a19b","f67456d74b418241"]}